# UPGRADE-19
# Autonomous Project Bootstrap & Developer Experience
#
# One-command repository onboarding,
# stack/framework detection,
# validation discovery,
# local model selection,
# project quality profiles,
# RAG bootstrap,
# MCP/tool discovery,
# AGENTS.md generation,
# safe configuration generation,
# baseline verification,
# readiness scoring,
# and zero-cost autonomous first task.
#
# PRIMARY PRINCIPLES
#
# NO-COST FIRST
# LOCAL-FIRST
# DRY-RUN FIRST
# NO SILENT REPOSITORY MUTATION
# NO SILENT MODEL DOWNLOAD
# NO SILENT PACKAGE INSTALL
# NO SILENT PAID FALLBACK
# NO INVENTED BUILD/TEST COMMANDS
# DETECT -> VERIFY -> PROPOSE -> APPLY

You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-18.

================================================================
MISSION
================================================================

The platform now reportedly contains:

- enterprise tenant/RLS architecture
- durable engineering jobs
- GitHub automation
- self-hosted/no-cost core
- local model gateway
- hardware profiler
- model factory
- RAG/indexing
- MCP
- local agent runtime
- model pool
- inference scheduler
- quality engineering
- model promotion/quarantine
- quality-first routing

Upgrade-19 must turn all of that into a coherent developer workflow.

Target user experience:

git clone REPOSITORY
cd REPOSITORY

zcoder init

        ↓

Repository Scanner
        ↓
Stack Detection
        ↓
Project Type
        ↓
Build/Test/Lint Discovery
        ↓
Security/Policy Discovery
        ↓
Hardware Detection
        ↓
Local Runtime Detection
        ↓
Installed Model Detection
        ↓
Model Recommendation
        ↓
Repository Index / RAG
        ↓
Tool / MCP / Skills Discovery
        ↓
Baseline Validation
        ↓
Quality Profile
        ↓
Generated Project Configuration
        ↓
Readiness Report

Then:

zcoder run "Fix the failing tests"

with a safe zero-cost local-first execution plan.

A developer should not need to manually configure twenty subsystems
before their first useful run.

================================================================
PHASE 0 — VERIFY UPGRADE-18
================================================================

Run:

git status --short
git log -30 --oneline
git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -30

python -m pytest -q -ra

python main.py --version
python -m build

git diff --check

Run current release gate.

Inspect:

local_ai_stack.py
no_cost_platform.py
agent_runtime.py
quality engineering code
project configuration code
skills.py
MCP modules
RAG/index modules
release_gate.py
CLI
tests/

Produce:

UPGRADE-18 EVIDENCE AUDIT

Capability
Claim
Actual Model Type
Actual Runtime
Fixture Type
Evidence Tier
Verdict

================================================================
1. CORRECT QUALITY EVIDENCE FIRST
================================================================

Upgrade-18 reportedly assigns:

qwen2.5-coder:7b
quality = 0.935
confidence = HIGH

Do not preserve HIGH confidence unless evidence proves:

actual model artifact
actual digest
actual runtime
actual generated output
actual benchmark fixture
actual validator execution

If deterministic FakeLocalModel or simulation produced it:

classify:

SIMULATED_MODEL

and downgrade confidence/evidence appropriately.

================================================================
2. CONFIDENCE ENUM CORRECTION
================================================================

Do not mix:

confidence

with:

severity.

Use confidence:

LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH

Use separate severity:

INFO
WARNING
HIGH
CRITICAL

A quarantined model does not have:

confidence = CRITICAL

unless "CRITICAL" belongs to a separately named severity field.

================================================================
3. PROJECT BOOTSTRAP SERVICE
================================================================

Create:

ProjectBootstrapService

Responsibilities:

scan
detect
verify
recommend
generate plan
apply approved bootstrap
baseline
index
profile
readiness

It should orchestrate existing subsystem services.

Do not duplicate their core logic.

================================================================
4. BOOTSTRAP PHASES
================================================================

Use explicit stages:

DISCOVER
ANALYZE
VERIFY
PLAN
APPLY
VALIDATE
INDEX
READY

Persist stage/results where useful.

================================================================
5. BOOTSTRAP MUST BE RESUMABLE
================================================================

If bootstrap fails at:

INDEX

rerunning must not recreate every configuration blindly.

Operations must be idempotent.

================================================================
6. DRY-RUN DEFAULT
================================================================

Primary behavior:

zcoder init

should detect/analyze and propose.

Repository mutation should require:

zcoder init --apply

or equivalent explicit action.

Follow existing CLI conventions if different.

================================================================
7. NO SILENT FILE CREATION
================================================================

Before writing:

AGENTS.md
.zcoder/*
configuration

show planned files and whether they:

CREATE
UPDATE
LEAVE_UNCHANGED

================================================================
8. EXISTING CONFIG SAFETY
================================================================

Never overwrite existing:

AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
README
CI configuration
editor config
project tool config

without merge strategy and explicit permission.

